<title>USA: U.S. interest rates mostly lower in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. interest rates mostly lower in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve</p>
<p>announced average interest rates for the week ended May 30,</p>
<p>compared with the May 23 week, as follows:</p>
<p>   Federal funds rate.................5.43 vs 5.52</p>
<p>   3-month Treasury bills.............4.94 vs 5.10</p>
<p>   3-month commercial paper...........5.67 vs 5.70</p>
<p>   3-month bankers acceptances........5.59 vs 5.63</p>
<p>   3-month CDs........................5.69 vs 5.71</p>
<p>   3-month Eurodollar.................5.69 vs 5.70</p>
<p>   30-year Government bond............6.99 vs 6.96</p>
</text>
